-| TD-16 | Replay verification | **Partially closed in this lane; `EvidenceCache` is kept.** `hephaestus-arena` gained history-borrowing `_in` verification entry points (`load_operator_evaluation_in`, `verify_selection_event_in`, `verify_reference_output_invariant_event_in`, `verify_cluster_event_in`, `load_recorded_evaluation_in`, backed by a new `hephaestus_ledger::EventIndex`) that verify against a caller-supplied, already hash-chain-verified history and the daemon's already-open artifact store instead of reopening stores and replaying the ledger per event, so a *full* verification pass (a cache miss, daemon startup, or explicit `replay`) is now linear in history size instead of quadratic. Measurement showed that removing `EvidenceCache` outright made `meta_evaluate_shows_a_descendant_strategy_reaching_equal_champions_at_lower_cost` alone take over 600 s (versus ~370 s for the entire 123-test control suite beforehand), because `refresh_projection` runs many times as history grows and summing a linear pass over each of those refreshes is still quadratic in the total event count. `EvidenceCache` was therefore kept, now layered on top of the cheaper linear verifiers, so a warm refresh still skips already-verified events at O(1) per event and a cold path (a new event, startup, or `replay`) is linear rather than quadratic. The original limitation is unchanged: an artifact blob in the CAS tampered with after its event was cached is not re-detected until the cache is cleared (daemon restart or `replay`); the ledger hash chain itself is still independently re-verified on every refresh via `EventLedger::replay_verified()`, so a rewritten ledger row is always caught immediately. | Before this lane, every refresh (cache hit or not) reopened `EvaluationStores` and replayed the ledger multiple times per evidence event, so even a cache *miss* cost grew superlinearly with history: a refresh took 1.3 s at 139 events, and meta-evaluation runs spun for minutes. | Remaining: close the CAS-tamper detection gap without reintroducing the quadratic blowup — e.g. invalidate a cached entry when its artifact content hash last-verified digest is cheap to recheck, or periodically force a bounded number of cache entries to fully re-verify each refresh. |
+| TD-16 | Replay verification | **Partially closed in this lane; `EvidenceCache` is kept.** `hephaestus-arena` gained history-borrowing `_in` verification entry points (`load_operator_evaluation_in`, `verify_selection_event_in`, `verify_reference_output_invariant_event_in`, `verify_cluster_event_in`, `load_recorded_evaluation_in`, backed by a new `hephaestus_ledger::EventIndex`) that verify against a caller-supplied, already hash-chain-verified history and the daemon's already-open artifact store instead of reopening stores and replaying the ledger per event, so a *full* verification pass (a cache miss, daemon startup, or explicit `replay`) is now linear in history size instead of quadratic. Measurement showed that removing `EvidenceCache` outright made `meta_evaluate_shows_a_descendant_strategy_reaching_equal_champions_at_lower_cost` alone take over 600 s (versus ~370 s for the entire 123-test control suite beforehand), because `refresh_projection` runs many times as history grows and summing a linear pass over each of those refreshes is still quadratic in the total event count. `EvidenceCache` was therefore kept, now layered on top of the cheaper linear verifiers, so a warm refresh still skips already-verified events at O(1) per event and a cold path (a new event, startup, or `replay`) is linear rather than quadratic. The original limitation is unchanged: an artifact blob in the CAS tampered with after its event was cached is not re-detected until the cache is cleared (daemon restart or `replay`); the ledger hash chain itself is still independently re-verified on every refresh via `EventLedger::replay_verified()`, so a rewritten ledger row is always caught immediately. **Further reduced in a later lane (Arena job pipeline speed-up):** `refresh_projection`'s per-call cost was already linear thanks to the above, but `service_async_messages`'s evidence loop still called it once per `ensure_capacity`/trace request from an active Arena trial — several per trial (`ensure_capacity`, `LifecycleStarted`, the completion trace) — so a full replay-and-reverify still ran several times per trial instead of once. The evidence loop now only durably persists the trace (the executor is acknowledged immediately, unchanged) and sets `arena_evidence_dirty`; `service_arena_message` flushes the deferred refresh exactly once, right before it handles the next Arena worker message, so every trial's evidence is still fully re-verified, just once per trial instead of once per trace. `self.state` itself was never stale in between, since every append site already applies its own event with `ControlState::apply` directly; only the batch of expensive re-verification passes (`EventLedger::replay_verified`, every `verify_*_history` call, `ControlState::from_events`) was deferred and coalesced. The direct (non-Arena) async job path is unchanged and still refreshes once per evidence event, since it was out of scope for that lane. Measured on `forge_assessment_records_verified_child_selection_and_replays` (two paired jobs, 8 trials total): `refresh_projection` calls dropped from 33 to 17, with per-call cost still growing with history size (roughly 30 ms to 250 ms across the run), confirming call count, not per-call cost, was the remaining lever. | Before this lane, every refresh (cache hit or not) reopened `EvaluationStores` and replayed the ledger multiple times per evidence event, so even a cache *miss* cost grew superlinearly with history: a refresh took 1.3 s at 139 events, and meta-evaluation runs spun for minutes. Later, even with the linear verifiers above, an Arena job's evidence loop still called `refresh_projection` several times per trial instead of once, so its cost was still counted (and paid) more often than the pipeline needed. | Remaining: close the CAS-tamper detection gap without reintroducing the quadratic blowup — e.g. invalidate a cached entry when its artifact content hash last-verified digest is cheap to recheck, or periodically force a bounded number of cache entries to fully re-verify each refresh. Also consider extending the same per-step batching to the direct (non-Arena) async job's evidence loop, and to admission/registration commands that each still call `refresh_projection` once even when appending several events in a row. |
